\b DETAILED SERVICE ADVISOR REPORT\b0\par
Application: DMS Auto Service Workflow System\par
Report Date: 2026-08-06\par
\par
\b 1. Executive Summary\b0\par
1.1 This application gives the Service Advisor (SA) one connected workflow from customer reception to final billing and printout.\par
1.2 The system reduces manual encoding, repeated lookups, and billing errors by linking customer, vehicle, service, parts, and transaction data.\par
1.3 The app supports both operations speed and front-desk control by combining searchable records, guided forms, and printable outputs.\par
\par
\b 2. Complete List of What a Service Advisor Can Do in This App\b0\par
2.1 Log in using SA access level and work inside the SA interface with role-based navigation.\par
2.2 Open the SA dashboard and monitor live totals for work orders, customers, and vehicles.\par
2.3 Open Work Order Transactions hub to access work orders, customers, closed billing search, and pricing from one screen.\par
2.4 Create a new work order with customer, vehicle, branch, technician, advisor name, status, and job description.\par
2.5 Reuse data by copying from an existing work order to speed repeat jobs and return visits.\par
2.6 Auto-create a customer when a new customer name is entered and no existing record is matched.\par
2.7 Auto-create or update a vehicle record from work order inputs (brand, model, year, plate, type).\par
2.8 Use brand and model catalog support to reduce wrong vehicle entries during intake.\par
2.9 Require unit type selection before work order creation to standardize service pricing behavior.\par
2.10 Edit work order information while order is still open, in-progress, or completed (before closure).\par
2.11 Record and update service advisor name, technician name, and job timing fields.\par
2.12 Capture automatic Time In when technician is assigned and no manual Time In is provided.\par
2.13 Define service lines with reason, required service description, labor amount, parts, unit price, and quantity.\par
2.14 Add or remove multiple service rows dynamically for complex repairs.\par
2.15 Auto-compute line totals and grand total in the service form while encoding.\par
2.16 Auto-suggest labor pricing from pricing rules or CSV data based on service required and unit type.\par
2.17 Keep service notes and work order notes in the same operational record.\par
2.18 Open technician print view to issue a technician-facing work order print without exposing pricing.\par
2.19 Prevent technician print if technician is not yet assigned, enforcing dispatch discipline.\par
2.20 Open billing statement page with complete customer, vehicle, and service line financial details.\par
2.21 See automatic Labor Total, Parts Total, Subtotal, VAT, and Grand Total computation.\par
2.22 Final-print billing and automatically set work order status to closed.\par
2.23 Auto-set Time Out at final print when missing, preserving complete cycle timing.\par
2.24 Search closed work orders from the transaction page using work order number, customer, plate, or vehicle.\par
2.25 Reopen the correct billing statement quickly for reprint or customer follow-up.\par
2.26 View transaction database records in tabular form with service counts, parts counts, totals, and timeline fields.\par
2.27 Open transaction detail view with separate Header, Services, and Parts tabs for fast review.\par
2.28 Export transaction records to CSV for reporting and external processing.\par
2.29 Manage customer master list: create, view, edit, and delete customer records.\par
2.30 Manage vehicle master list: create, view, edit, and delete vehicle records.\par
2.31 Access parts database operations: create, edit, delete parts entries and track transaction type.\par
2.32 Search and filter parts records by keyword and transaction type (NewEntry, Restock, PriceEdit, Sold).\par
2.33 Use helper page global search across customers, vehicles, work orders, pricing, technicians/advisors, parts usage, and transaction records.\par
2.34 Sort helper results by relevance, date (newest or oldest), A-Z, and Z-A depending on query need.\par
2.35 Use fullscreen mode from header for distraction reduction in front-desk operations.\par
2.36 Log out securely from the header after shift or station handoff.\par
\par
\b 3. How This App Supports the Service Advisor Role\b0\par
3.1 Workflow Integration Support\par
3.1.1 Intake, dispatch, service definition, billing, and history retrieval are in one connected process.\par
3.1.2 SA does not need to maintain separate spreadsheets to complete the core service cycle.\par
3.2 Speed and Throughput Support\par
3.2.1 Auto-linking customer and vehicle data reduces repeated typing.\par
3.2.2 Copy-from-existing-work-order and searchable closed-order retrieval reduce turnaround time for repeat concerns.\par
3.2.3 Dynamic service rows and automatic calculations reduce hand-calculator dependency.\par
3.3 Accuracy and Compliance Support\par
3.3.1 Standardized work order numbering and status flow reduce tracking ambiguity.\par
3.3.2 Closure lock behavior prevents accidental edits on already closed billing records.\par
3.3.3 VAT and total computation logic reduce billing miscalculation risk.\par
3.3.4 Technician-required rule before technician print supports accountable work dispatch.\par
3.4 Communication and Coordination Support\par
3.4.1 Technician print format shares work instructions clearly while hiding customer billing prices.\par
3.4.2 Transaction and helper searches let SA answer customer follow-up questions quickly.\par
3.4.3 Technician summary tables support quick visibility of assignments and current workload.\par
3.5 Data Continuity Support\par
3.5.1 Every important work order state change can generate transaction records.\par
3.5.2 Historical records can be reviewed by table or per-record detail tabs.\par
3.5.3 CSV export allows backup reporting and business analysis outside the app when needed.\par
\par
\b 4. Ergonomic Alignment with the Service Advisor Work Area\b0\par
4.1 Cognitive Ergonomics (Mental Load Reduction)\par
4.1.1 The app groups tasks by practical station flow: dashboard to work order to service to billing to history.\par
4.1.2 Form defaults, data reuse, and auto-computation lower memory burden and reduce decision fatigue.\par
4.1.3 Search-centered helper tools reduce context switching to paper notes or external files.\par
4.2 Physical Ergonomics (Keyboard and Mouse Efficiency)\par
4.2.1 Single-screen action links (Information, Services, Print WO, Billing) reduce click travel between modules.\par
4.2.2 Dynamic row editing reduces repeated page reloads for multi-line jobs.\par
4.2.3 Fullscreen mode supports better visibility on reception counters and shared terminals.\par
4.3 Temporal Ergonomics (Time Pressure Handling)\par
4.3.1 Rapid closed-order search supports customer waiting scenarios at release time.\par
4.3.2 Automatic Time In and Time Out capture improves timestamp consistency under busy conditions.\par
4.3.3 Reminder prompts in work-order transactions support attention recovery for pending calls and approvals.\par
4.4 Team Ergonomics (Coordination and Handover)\par
4.4.1 Technician assignment visibility and print gating improve SA-to-technician handoff quality.\par
4.4.2 Structured service lines and notes improve clarity during shift change or audit review.\par
4.4.3 Role-based access keeps SA workspace focused while preserving admin and GM boundaries.\par
\par
\b 5. Practical SA Use Pattern (Recommended Day Flow)\b0\par
5.1 Start shift: log in as SA, open dashboard, check active counts and technician panel.\par
5.2 During intake: create work order, verify customer and vehicle, select unit type, assign technician, capture concern.\par
5.3 During service authoring: open Services, encode lines, validate auto-pricing, review totals.\par
5.4 Before release: open Billing, verify customer and vehicle identity, confirm VAT and grand total.\par
5.5 At release: final print billing to close order and capture missing Time Out automatically.\par
5.6 After release: use transaction and history views for reprint, disputes, or follow-up inquiries.\par
\par
\b 6. High-Value Outcomes for Service Advisor Performance\b0\par
6.1 Faster intake and release with fewer manual steps.\par
6.2 Better billing accuracy and fewer recalculation mistakes.\par
6.3 Clearer technician instructions and stronger dispatch control.\par
6.4 Improved customer response time using centralized searchable records.\par
6.5 Better shift handover through consistent, structured, and printable documentation.\par
\par
\b 7. Conclusion\b0\par
7.1 This DMS implementation is strongly aligned with SA front-desk operations by combining workflow speed, data control, print-ready outputs, and search-driven support.\par
7.2 The application supports both productivity and ergonomic fit for daily high-volume service advising tasks.\par
